the date of last reported is The "" date last active '' on a credit report refers to the last time an account was used or had activity reported to the credit bureau. This date is important because it can help lenders and other creditors determine how recently you have used your credit and how active your credit accounts are. 

For example, if you have a credit card that you haven't used in several years, the "" date last active '' on that account will be several years ago. On the other hand, if you have a credit card that you use regularly, the "" date last active '' will be more recent. 

The "" date last active '' is just one of several factors that creditors and lenders use to evaluate your creditworthiness. Other factors include your payment history, credit utilization, length of credit history, and the types of credit accounts you have. 

Last Reported : transunion XX/XX/XXXX XXXX XXXX this date of last reported is re-aging as well because it makes the 7 year tennessee collection rule dropping off my credit report in XXXX on transunion and XXXX on XXXX 

Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), re-aging a credit account is illegal. Specifically, the FCRA requires that accurate information be reported on credit reports, and prohibits the intentional reporting of inaccurate information. If a credit account is re-aged, it may be considered inaccurate information and may be subject to legal action. 

Re-aging refers to changing the date of last activity on a credit account to make it appear more recent than it actually is. This practice is also sometimes called "" resetting the clock '' or "" flipping the date. '' Re-aging can be used to make an old delinquency appear more recent, which can negatively impact a person 's credit score and creditworthiness. Re-aging is often done by debt collectors or credit repair companies, who may try to convince a consumer to make a small payment on an old debt in order to restart the clock on the debt 's age.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,"TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.",TN,381XX,,Web,2023-05-03,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
