7044501,2023-05-30,"Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports",Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"CC : Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ( CFPB ) CC : South Carolina Attorney General ( Complaint Filed ) CC : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX CC : Federal Trade Commission ( FTC ) CC : XXXX, XXXX, Transunion Dear XXXX ( Original Creditor : XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX  ), I am writing to dispute the charge-off that appears on my credit report for account XXXX. I believe that this charge-off was the result of multiple violations of federal law, including the Uninformed Decision Law ( 15 U.S. Code 1601 ( a ), the Lack of Evidence of Indebtedness Law ( 15 U.S. Code 1602 ( g ) ( 2 ), and the Adequate Notice Law ( 1643 of 15 U.S. Code 1602 ( k ). Therefore, I am requesting that it be removed from my credit report. 

